specifies where the report will be written to.  Depending on  the
chosen format, this may refer to a single file or to a directory.
For  those  formats  that write to a single file, specifying a as
the path will redirect the report to the  standard  output.   The
following  output formats are allowed: A machine‐parseable Comma‐
Separated Values (CSV) file.  This file contains the results  for
all  test  cases  and test programs.  Test cases are logged using
the following syntax: tc, duration, test‐program, test‐case,  re‐
sult[,  reason]  The field for test cases is always one of or The
last two are always followed by  a  reason.   Test  programs  are
logged with the following syntax: tp, duration, test‐program, re‐
sult[,  reason]  In  this  case, the can be one of: which denotes
test programs that ran without any failure; which refers to  test
programs  in  which  one or more test cases failed; or which men‐
tions those test programs that failed to execute by some  reason.
The  reason  field  is only available in the last case.  The time
required to execute each test case and test program is also  pro‐
vided.   You  should  not rely on the order of the entries in the
resulting output.  A user‐friendly report that shows the progress
of the test suite’s execution as it operates.  This type  of  re‐
port  should  always  be  redirected to a virtual terminal, not a
file, as it may use control sequences that will make  the  output
unreadable  in regular files.  A report contained in a single XML
file.  Ideal for later processing with to generate nice HTML  re‐
ports.   The  most  simple way of running a test suite is to pipe
the output of through without any additional  flags.   This  will
use  the  default output format, which is suitable to most users:
atf‐run | atf‐report In some situations, it may be interesting to
get a machine‐parseable file  aside  from  the  standard  report.
This  can  be  done as follows: atf‐run | atf‐report ‐o csv:test‐
suite.csv ‐o ticker:‐ Or if the standard report is  not  desired,
thus  achieving completely silent operation: atf‐run | atf‐report
‐o csv:testsuite.csv
